E AX3033 585-multi-rule-misuse.ax:38:8-17 macro-unreachable-rule "macro `sameArity` has a rule that can never match: rule 2 is shadowed by rule 1" !"rules are tried IN ORDER and the first whose pattern matches wins (macro-system.md MAC-LANG-18); an earlier rule of the same arity whose elements are all plain binders matches every invocation of that arity, so nothing of that arity after it is reachable" ?"give the earlier rule a pattern that can FAIL - a literal, or a parenthesised shape of two or more elements - or delete this one. A one-element `(p)` is the bare binder `p`: the parentheses are the same ones an argument loses, so it still matches everything"
E AX3018 585-multi-rule-misuse.ax:54:2-8 macro-arity "no rule of macro `spread` matches this invocation; it accepts (spread T) or (spread T a b)" !"rules are tried IN ORDER and the first whose pattern matches wins (macro-system.md MAC-LANG-18): an invocation matching none is this refusal rather than a fall-through. A plain identifier in a shape matches any argument; a literal matches its own VALUE, and a parenthesised shape matches a form of that many elements - but not a form headed by a keyword (`if`, `let`, `lambda`, `match`), which the parser gives a shape of its own" ?"write the invocation in one of the shapes above"
